--- machine\software\radius
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius

Configuration of the radiusd RADIUS authentication service.

Administrators own these keys; radiusd needs read and subtree-notify access.
It has no configuration-write authority. Configuration is watched and
revalidated periodically, including referenced files. Invalid, unreadable, or
pending configuration pauses successful admissions. Registry names, values and
layer selection are read through one bounded read-only snapshot. Its handle is
closed before credential files are opened. Use administrative transactions for
related edits and immutable prepared files for referenced credentials.

--- machine\software\radius\settings
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings

Listener addresses and bounded authentication-conversation resources.

--- machine\software\radius\settings listen
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings Listen
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–16 distinct literal IPv4 or IPv6 socket addresses with nonzero ports
applies: live

UDP listeners, such as 0.0.0.0:1812 and [::]:1812.

IPv6 sockets are IPv6-only. Hostnames and mapped IPv6 addresses are refused.
The service SID also needs PORT_BIND in the normal port-reservation SD.
Changing the listener set cancels pending exchanges and cached replies.

--- machine\software\radius\settings idletimeoutseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings IdleTimeoutSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 30
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new exchanges)

Maximum inactivity during an authentication conversation.

--- machine\software\radius\settings overalltimeoutseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings OverallTimeoutSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 120
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new exchanges)

Fixed total conversation lifetime, including time spent waiting for authd.

Progress and configuration changes never extend an existing deadline.

--- machine\software\radius\settings replycacheseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings ReplyCacheSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 15
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new cache entries)

Lifetime of exact retransmission replies.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxattempts
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxAttempts
type: REG_DWORD
default: 256
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Global bound on allocated authentication conversations.

Lowering this bound stops new allocation without extending existing work.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxattemptsperclient
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxAttemptsPerClient
type: REG_DWORD
default: 32
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Conversation allocation bound per trusted client definition.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxcachedreplies
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxCachedReplies
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1024
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Maximum cached RADIUS replies; oldest entries are evicted at capacity.

--- machine\software\radius\settings fragmentbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings FragmentBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1000
valid: 64–3000
applies: live (new exchanges)

Maximum outgoing EAP-TTLS fragment payload.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxverifications
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxVerifications
type: REG_DWORD
default: 32
valid: 1–MaxAttempts
applies: live

Maximum simultaneous asynchronous authd credential verifications.

At capacity a newly verification-ready attempt fails without keys. There is
no unbounded queue. Lowering the limit does not restart existing work.

--- machine\software\radius\settings schemaversion
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings SchemaVersion
type: REG_DWORD
default: (required)
valid: 3
applies: live

Configuration schema version. Older layouts require explicit conversion.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxstages
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxStages
type: REG_DWORD
default: 32
valid: 4–256
applies: live (new exchanges)

Maximum milestone records emitted for one authentication attempt.

The final summary is separate and includes a truncation marker when the stage bound omitted milestones.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxeventbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxEventBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 8192
valid: 1024–32768
applies: live

Maximum encoded diagnostic event payload, in bytes.

Oversized summaries shed optional fields and carry a truncation marker. An event that still exceeds the bound is omitted and counted as failed.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticseventspersecond
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsEventsPerSecond
type: REG_DWORD
default: 200
valid: 1–100000
applies: live

Ordinary diagnostic event budget per one-second window.

Milestones and drop reports share this budget. DiagnosticsSummaryReserve provides additional final-summary and collection-report capacity.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticssummaryreserve
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsSummaryReserve
type: REG_DWORD
default: 50
valid: 1–100000
applies: live

Additional final-summary and collection-report budget per one-second window.

Reserved capacity is consumed first for summaries. They may also use the ordinary budget. Neither budget guarantees delivery under overload.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsdropsamples
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsDropSamples
type: REG_DWORD
default: 8
valid: 0–1024
applies: live

Maximum source samples retained across drop buckets per report interval.

Zero disables personal samples while retaining aggregate counts. A bucket carries at most one recent source and matched-client sample.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsreportseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsReportSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 5
valid: 1–3600
applies: live

Diagnostic collection and drop report interval, in seconds.

Emission is best effort. Collection counters are cumulative since startup; drop bucket counts cover the preceding interval.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticslookbackseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsLookbackSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 900
valid: 1–DiagnosticsMaxLookbackSeconds
applies: live (new reader)

Default diagnostic history lookback, in seconds.

The value must not exceed DiagnosticsMaxLookbackSeconds.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxlookbackseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxLookbackSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 86400
valid: 1–2592000
applies: live (new reader)

Maximum requested diagnostic history lookback, in seconds.

eventd retention and authorization independently determine the available evidence.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxrecords
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxRecords
type: REG_DWORD
default: 4096
valid: 16–65536
applies: live (new reader)

Maximum records requested per query and retained by a live reader.

Reaching the bound marks the result as limited. Filters for personal and configuration fields operate on this returned record window.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxattempts
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxAttempts
type: REG_DWORD
default: 200
valid: 1–10000
applies: live (new reader)

Maximum reconstructed attempts displayed by one reader.

The retained record and payload limits apply independently.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsmaxviewbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsMaxViewBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 4194304
valid: 65536–67108864
applies: live (new reader)

Maximum retained diagnostic record payload and deduplication-key bytes.

The same bound limits each encoded eventd response frame before allocation. Decoding and collection structures require additional memory.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsbackfillseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsBackfillSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 60
valid: 1–86400
applies: live (new reader)

Minimum overlapping history requested after a stream interruption, in seconds.

The actual query uses the larger of this interval and its original lookback, capped by DiagnosticsMaxLookbackSeconds. Recovered records are deduplicated; continuity is not guaranteed.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsreconnectseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsReconnectSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 3
valid: 1–300
applies: live (new reader)

Delay before reconnecting a diagnostic stream, in seconds.

Authentication does not wait for diagnostic recovery.

--- machine\software\radius\settings diagnosticsstreamseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings DiagnosticsStreamSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 60
valid: 5–3600
applies: live (new reader)

Maximum diagnostic stream connection lifetime, in seconds.

The reader renews the caller-authorized query with overlapping history. Renewal and missing evidence are shown as possible gaps.

--- machine\software\radius\accessprofiles\<guid>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessProfiles\<guid>

Complete access settings selected by assignment rules. `Name` is a display
label; `Enabled` is `0` or `1`. References use the permanent UUIDv4 key name.
Unknown profile values invalidate the configuration. Disabling a selected
profile refuses the affected admission.

--- machine\software\radius\accessprofiles\<guid> vlanid
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessProfiles\<guid> VlanId
type: REG_DWORD
default: (absent, no VLAN override)
valid: 1–4094
applies: live (subsequent authentication)

VLAN sent with the complete tunnel attribute set in an Access-Accept.
Zero is invalid. Removing the value stops sending VLAN override attributes.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<guid>\rules\<rule-guid>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<guid>\Rules\<rule-guid>

PNP-style assignment rule. Child rule keys are exceptions to this rule.
`Name` is an optional display label. `Enabled` defaults to `1`; `0` hides the
whole subtree. `Priority` is a signed decimal string or DWORD and inherits
from the parent, or defaults to `0` at a root.

`Actions` is a string or string list containing `ASSIGN(profile-guid)`,
`REJECT` or `NULL`. The absent action abstains. Matching children shadow
their parent; abstaining descendants use the nearest ancestor decision.
The highest priority wins. Equal-priority rejection wins over assignment.
Equally ranked different profiles refuse the affected connection.

Condition values use `Fact.Operator` names. Supported families are
`Subject.User`, `Subject.Group`, `Subject.Name`,
`Subject.Claim.<name>.<type>`, `Client.Id`, `Client.Address`,
`Request.SSID` and `Request.Station`. Operators are `Equal`, `Present`,
and numeric `GreaterThan` or `LessThan`. Claim types preserve native values.
`Present=0` cannot match a claim whose absence authd has not established.
Unknown facts and unsupported operators invalidate configuration.

Rules are bounded to 1024, with 32 exception levels, 64 conditions per rule,
256 alternatives per condition and 4 MiB of aggregate rule values.
No selected profile refuses access. Defaults require an explicit rule.
Assignment never bypasses credentials, Connect permissions or allowances.

Objects use canonical lowercase UUIDv4 key names. Display names are separate,
may change, and need not be unique. At most 256 objects of each kind are accepted.
An empty object collection is valid and grants no access through that collection.

--- machine\software\radius\settings statussecurity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings StatusSecurity
type: REG_SZ or REG_BINARY
default: SYSTEM and Administrators may query
valid: SDDL or binary security descriptor with an owner
applies: live (next local status request)

Descriptor for the local status query right, mask 0x1.

Generic read and all map to Query; generic write and execute map to zero.
The kernel-attested peer token is checked; Unix IDs do not authorize requests.
Unreadable or malformed explicit descriptors deny queries. This object grants
no Registry write authority or service-control rights.

--- machine\software\radius\serveridentities\<identity>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\ServerIdentities\<identity>

A named certificate chain and matching private key.

--- machine\software\radius\serveridentities\<identity> name
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\ServerIdentities\<identity> Name
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty display name, at most 256 bytes; no control characters
applies: live

Friendly display label. References use the immutable GUID, not this name.

--- machine\software\radius\serveridentities\<identity> certificatefiles
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\ServerIdentities\<identity> CertificateFiles
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–16 absolute DER certificate paths, each at most 65536 bytes
applies: live

Ordered certificate chain, starting with the server certificate.

--- machine\software\radius\serveridentities\<identity> privatekeyfile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\ServerIdentities\<identity> PrivateKeyFile
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: absolute path to an unencrypted DER private key, at most 65536 bytes
applies: live

Private key matching the leaf certificate. Management import accepts PEM or
DER and stores protected DER files.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client>

A trusted RADIUS client selected by the actual UDP source address.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> name
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Name
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty display name, at most 256 bytes; no control characters
applies: live

Friendly display label. References use the immutable GUID, not this name.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> enabled
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Enabled
type: REG_DWORD
default: (required)
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

A disabled client denies affected requests without a broader-prefix fallback.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> addresses
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Addresses
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–256 canonical literal IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDR prefixes
applies: live

Most-specific prefixes select a client. Disabled clients and wrong secrets
have no fallback to less-specific clients. Equal prefixes are invalid.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> secretfile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> SecretFile
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: absolute path to a protected regular file containing 16–1024 bytes
applies: live

The management program generates 48-character secrets by default. Explicit
reveal requires file-read authority. Ordinary output omits secret contents.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> policies
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Policies
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–256 existing access-policy GUIDs with distinct SSIDs
applies: live

The integrity-checked Called-Station-Id must identify an exact allowed SSID.
NAS attributes cannot select a trusted client.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy>

Admission policy, independently of credential verification in authd.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> name
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> Name
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty display name, at most 256 bytes; no control characters
applies: live

Friendly display label. References use the immutable GUID, not this name.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> enabled
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> Enabled
type: REG_DWORD
default: (required)
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

A disabled policy denies new admissions for its SSID.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> ssid
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> SSID
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty UTF-8 text, at most 32 bytes
applies: live

Changing the SSID invalidates conversations bound to its previous value.
Display-name changes preserve identity.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> connectsecurity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> ConnectSecurity
type: REG_SZ or REG_BINARY
default: (required)
valid: SDDL or validated self-relative SD with owner, at most 65536 bytes
applies: live

The verified subject is checked for Connect, mask 0x1. Missing subject context
cannot grant admission. The kernel query creates no token or impersonation
authority. This descriptor is separate from Registry management permissions.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> authenticationprofile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> AuthenticationProfile
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: existing authentication-profile GUID
applies: live

Reference to reusable methods and server identity. Each policy retains its
own Connect descriptor.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> reauthenticateseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> ReauthenticateSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: (required)
valid: 1–4294967295
applies: live

Successful admissions request periodic reauthentication using Session-Timeout
and Termination-Action. Existing access is not immediately disconnected;
actual client enforcement must be qualified. Management defaults to 3600.

--- machine\software\radius\authenticationprofiles\<profile>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AuthenticationProfiles\<profile>

Reusable method settings, separate from admission permissions.

--- machine\software\radius\authenticationprofiles\<profile> name
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AuthenticationProfiles\<profile> Name
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty display name, at most 256 bytes; no control characters
applies: live

Friendly display label. References use the immutable GUID, not this name.

--- machine\software\radius\authenticationprofiles\<profile> enabled
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AuthenticationProfiles\<profile> Enabled
type: REG_DWORD
default: (required)
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

A disabled shared profile disables admission through its referring policies.

--- machine\software\radius\authenticationprofiles\<profile> authenticationmethods
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AuthenticationProfiles\<profile> AuthenticationMethods
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–2 unique entries from ttls-pap, peap-mschapv2
applies: live

Ordered allowed methods; the first is preferred. PEAP/MSCHAPv2 requires authd
credential support and uses TLS 1.2. radiusd receives no reusable NT hash.
TTLS/PAP supports TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3. EAP-TLS remains future work.

--- machine\software\radius\authenticationprofiles\<profile> serveridentity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AuthenticationProfiles\<profile> ServerIdentity
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: existing server-identity GUID
applies: live

Reference to the certificate chain and matching private key used for TLS
authentication through this profile.

Referenced credential files must be singly linked regular files, owned by SYSTEM
or Administrators, and protected against modification by other principals.
The service may read them. Private keys and shared secrets may grant read access
only to SYSTEM, Administrators, and radiusd. Public certificates may be readable
by others. Files are opened without following a final symlink.

Prepare protected files before transactionally publishing references. Failed
management saves remove their newly staged files. Successful replacements retain
previous files until they can safely be removed. Certificate replacement cancels
affected unfinished conversations and cached replies.

Missing references, malformed values, and unreadable credentials invalidate the
complete candidate. radiusd pauses admission rather than keeping old policy
active, while its local status endpoint remains available for diagnosis and
repair. Intentionally disabled, otherwise valid objects do not invalidate
unrelated policy. Direct Registry edits can bypass management deletion checks.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingenabled
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingEnabled
type: REG_DWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether the durable accounting service receives reports.

The private directory and accounting UDP port permission must be provisioned before activation.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountinglisten
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingListen
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: 0.0.0.0:1813
valid: 1–16 literal, nonoverlapping IPv4 or IPv6 socket addresses
applies: live

Accounting UDP listener addresses.

IPv6 sockets are IPv6-only. Mapped addresses, duplicate listeners, overlapping wildcard bindings, and zero ports are refused.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingsettings
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingSettings
type: REG_SZ
default: {}
valid: versioned Settings JSON with known fields and validated bounds
applies: live

Grouped accounting controls.

Individual Accounting values override the corresponding JSON fields. AccountingEnabled supplies the final enabled state. Unknown JSON fields are refused.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingsecurity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingSecurity
type: REG_SZ or REG_BINARY
default: O:SYG:SYD:(A;;0x3f;;;SY)(A;;0x3f;;;BA)
valid: SDDL or validated self-relative SD with owner
applies: live

Default authority for protected accounting operations.

Rights are Read 0x1, Personal 0x2, Usage 0x4, Disconnect 0x8, Correct 0x10, and Raw 0x20. Policy descriptors can delegate a narrower scope. Orphaned history uses this descriptor.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingselfservice
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingSelfService
type: REG_DWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether verified caller identity grants personal accounting views.

The actual peer token SID must match verified session identity. This grants no Disconnect, Correct, Raw, global status, or direct ledger-file access.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingbatchmilliseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingBatchMilliseconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1000
valid: 1–5000 milliseconds
applies: live

Maximum intentional wait before a pending report batch is committed.

The timer starts when the oldest report is queued. Count and byte pressure or another owner operation can flush earlier. Slow storage adds latency beyond this intentional wait.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingbatchcount
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingBatchCount
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 512
valid: 1–10000 reports, no greater than AccountingQueueCount
applies: live

Maximum reports in one durable transaction.

Increasing the value amortizes synchronization but increases batch work and reply bursts.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingbatchbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingBatchBytes
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1048576
valid: 4096–67108864 bytes
applies: live

Maximum serialized observation bytes in one batch.

An observation exceeding this bound is refused without acknowledgment. This bounds serialized observations, not every allocator or SQLite buffer.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingqueuecount
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingQueueCount
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 4096
valid: 1–65536 operations, at least AccountingBatchCount
applies: restart

Bound on queued ledger operations and pending UDP replies.

The queue is allocated at process startup. A live change remains unavailable until restart. Overflow produces no success accounting reply.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingmaxdatabasebytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingMaxDatabaseBytes
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1073741824
valid: 1048576–1125899906842624 bytes
applies: live

Limit on database pages used for admissions and report commits.

WAL, shared memory, and filesystem overhead require additional space. Free pages remain reusable. Lowering the value does not shrink allocated files. Preserve storage headroom for maintenance and recovery.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingretryhorizonseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRetryHorizonSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 86400
valid: 1–2592000 seconds
applies: live

Minimum retained semantic retry window.

Observation retention must cover this window. Changed identifiers and Acct-Delay-Time do not necessarily describe a new usage report.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingobservationretentionseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingObservationRetentionSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 604800
valid: retry horizon through summary retention, in seconds
applies: live

Age at which detailed observations become eligible for checkpointed expiry.

Maintenance removes bounded chunks. Quota evidence remains separate from personal history.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingsummaryretentionseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingSummaryRetentionSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 7776000
valid: observation retention through 316224000 seconds
applies: live

Retention period for ended personal session summaries.

Active sessions remain until actual or inferred end. Lifetime quota evidence can outlive summaries.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingdetailintervalseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingDetailIntervalSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 0
valid: 0 through summary retention, in seconds
applies: live

Coarseness of Interim history views.

Zero returns unsampled retained detail. A positive value returns the latest Interim per time bucket within the bounded query. Ingestion, retry evidence, and live quota interpretation remain exact.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingstaleseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingStaleSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1800
valid: 60 through AccountingExpireSeconds
applies: live

Report silence before an active session is marked stale.

Stale sessions continue consuming concurrent slots and time allowances until evidence or inferred expiration closes them.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingexpireseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingExpireSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 86400
valid: AccountingStaleSeconds through 316224000 seconds
applies: live

Report silence before an inferred session end.

An inferred end is uncertain evidence, not a factual Stop.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingreservationseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingReservationSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 120
valid: 10–3600 seconds
applies: live

Lifetime of an admission reservation without a session report.

Reservations commit before Access-Accept and prevent concurrent admissions from spending the same final slot.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingrequiremessageauthenticator
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRequireMessageAuthenticator
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether accounting requests must include Message-Authenticator.

Request-Authenticator is always verified. A supplied Message-Authenticator is always checked even when this control is zero.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingrawcapture
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRawCapture
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether development packet capture stores authenticated accounting packets.

Capture is separately bounded and requires names and attributes retention. Known credential and key attributes are refused before any observation is recorded.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingrawretentionseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRawRetentionSeconds
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 3600
valid: 0–86400 seconds
applies: live

Maximum age of development packet captures.

Maintenance removes eligible captures. This does not change normalized observation retention.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingrawmaxbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRawMaxBytes
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 67108864
valid: 0 through half AccountingMaxDatabaseBytes
applies: live

Maximum payload bytes retained as development packet captures.

Capture stops at the bound; accounting processing continues. Storage page overhead is additional.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountinglinkedviews
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingLinkedViews
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether related-session views can link verified principal occurrences.

Original session legs remain distinct. Linking uses verified identity and caller scope, never a reported username alone.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingretainnames
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRetainNames
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether future observations and grants retain account display names.

Turning this off removes reported usernames and canonical names from future ingest. It does not erase old records or SID-based quota evidence.

--- machine\software\radius\settings accountingretainattributes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings AccountingRetainAttributes
type: REG_DWORD or REG_SZ
default: 1
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether future observations retain opaque attribute detail.

Normalized session fields remain available. Turning this off is incompatible with raw capture and does not erase earlier detail.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> accountingprofile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> AccountingProfile
type: REG_SZ
default: (absent)
valid: enabled accounting-profile GUID or empty
applies: live

Declarative accounting normalization profile.

An absent or empty reference uses standard attributes. Rules cannot execute code or bypass peer integrity.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> disconnectport
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> DisconnectPort
type: REG_DWORD
default: 3799
valid: 1–65535
applies: live

UDP destination port for administrative and allowance-triggered Disconnect.

The destination address comes from the recorded source and must remain admitted by the same client prefix.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> servicekind
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> ServiceKind
type: REG_SZ
default: wifi
valid: wifi, accounting-only, or empty
applies: live

Service represented by an access policy.

Accounting-only policies need no SSID, Connect descriptor, or authentication profile. They accept accounting reports without implementing another authentication service.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> accountingrequired
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> AccountingRequired
type: REG_DWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether new admissions require available accounting.

Applicable principal allowances also require checked accounting unless the explicit outage mode permits bypass.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> onaccountingunavailable
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> OnAccountingUnavailable
type: REG_SZ
default: deny-new
valid: deny-new or allow-new
applies: live

Admission behavior when required accounting or applicable limits are unavailable.

Deny-new refuses admission. Allow-new permits admission without a reliable allowance check or reservation and increments a bypass counter. Neither mode acknowledges lost reports or creates a false Class mapping.

--- machine\software\radius\accesspolicies\<policy> accountingsecurity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccessPolicies\<policy> AccountingSecurity
type: REG_SZ or REG_BINARY
default: (inherit global AccountingSecurity)
valid: SDDL or validated self-relative SD with owner; empty inherits
applies: live

Authority for this policy's accounting history and actions.

Read, Personal, Usage, Disconnect, Correct, and Raw are independent rights. Registry management and network Connect permissions remain separate.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> principal
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Principal
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: canonical user or group SID
applies: live

Principal charged by an allowance.

Every applicable user and group allowance consumes the same attributable usage independently. Membership comes from verified authentication provenance.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> policy
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Policy
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: existing policy GUID or *
applies: live

Scope of an allowance.

An asterisk shares the allowance across policies. Delegated policy queries do not expose the global allowance.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> dimension
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Dimension
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: input-bytes, output-bytes, total-bytes, total-session-time, connected-time, concurrent
applies: live

Resource counted by an allowance.

Time dimensions use milliseconds. Total session time sums intervals; connected time unions them. Concurrent counts active and stale sessions plus unconsumed admission reservations.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> period
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Period
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: lifetime, day, week, month
applies: live

Calendar for an allowance.

Periods use UTC. Weeks start Monday. Concurrent permits lifetime only. Byte deltas spanning boundaries carry uncertain attribution.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> maximum
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Maximum
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: exact unsigned decimal through 18446744073709551615
applies: live

Maximum resource amount in an allowance period.

Zero denies the resource. Allowances do not add together; all applicable constraints must pass.

--- machine\software\radius\quotas\<quota> disconnect
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Quotas\<quota> Disconnect
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1
valid: 0 or 1
applies: live

Whether exhausted allowances request Disconnect for ongoing sessions.

Requests use durable bounded attempts. An ACK does not establish that a device ended its session.

--- machine\software\radius\accountingprofiles\<profile> definition
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\AccountingProfiles\<profile> Definition
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: version 1 JSON, at most 65536 bytes, 32 rules and 128 dictionary entries
applies: live

Bounded declarative accounting normalization rules.

Rules select standard or vendor attributes, decode bytes or unsigned integers, map bounded numeric values, and supply or replace named normalized fields. Targets and dictionary selectors must be unique. Executable plugins are not supported.
